# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Expo only exposes variables prefixed
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ to the app, and they are embedded in the JS bundle — treat every
# value here as public. Nothing secret belongs in this file; the backend holds
# the secrets (JWT_SECRET, eSewa keys, the Firebase service account).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Leave unset during development and the app derives the backend
# address from whatever host is serving the Metro bundle, so a phone on the
# same wifi connects with no configuration at all (see src/lib/config.ts).
#
# Set it when that guess is wrong — a tunnel, a staging server, a device on a
# different network. No trailing slash, and do not include /api.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.5:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase — only needed for Google sign-in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same project the web app uses. Copy these from the web app's .env,
# renaming the VITE_ prefix to EXPO_PUBLIC_ — the values are identical.
# Email/password sign-in works without any of this.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google OAuth client IDs — only needed for Google sign-in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Created in Google Cloud Console under the SAME project as Firebase. Each
# platform needs its own client ID; Google rejects a request that presents the
# wrong one. See the "Google sign-in setup" section of README.md for how to
# create these, including the SHA-1 fingerprint Android requires.
#
# Until these are filled in, the Google button is hidden rather than shown and
# failing on tap.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
